 34AL    U(P,34AL)                     2019Li41                  ENSDF    202609
 34AL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34AL c  2019Li41: {+34}Mg and {+34}Al ions were produced via fragmentation     
 34AL2c  reactions induced by a 1.4-GeV pulsed proton beam from the Proton      
 34AL3c  Synchrotron Booster on a UC{-x} target at ISOLDE-CERN. Th atoms that   
 34AL4c  diffused out of the target matrix were selectively laser ionized using 
 34AL5c  the resonance ionization laser ion source (RILIS) and accelerated to 40
 34AL6c  keV. A=34 nuclei were selected by the ISOLDE General Purpose Separator 
 34AL7c  and implanted onto a movable tape located at the center of the ISOLDE  
 34AL8c  Decay station. The {+34}Mg beam rate is 700 pps {I1} and the {+34}Al   
 34AL9c  beam rate is 800 pps {I1}, both with purities of >99%. |b particles    
 34ALAc  were detected using a 3-cm-thick NE102 plastic scintillator with an    
 34ALBc  efficiency of 90% {I5}. |g rays were detected using five HPGe clover   
 34ALCc  detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, |b|g-coin, |b|g|g-coin, and              
 34ALDc  |be{++}/e{+-}coin. Deduced levels, isomer, J, |p, decay branching      
 34ALEc  ratios, log {Ift}, T{-1/2} and %|b{+-}n of parent, and configuration   
 34ALFc  mixings. Comparisons with large-scale shell-model calculations using   
 34ALGc  the SDPF-U-MIX interaction.                                            
 34AL c  2001Nu01: 1-GeV proton beam on uranium carbide target at ISOLDE-CERN.  
 34AL c  1989Ba50: 600-MeV proton beam on uranium carbide target at ISOLDE-CERN.
